===The Tallest Hurdle===
A massive waterfall keeps all but the strongest Trainers from reaching the city. Use {{m|Waterfall|the HM move}} to climb the wall of water and reach the nearby Pokémon Center. Take a moment to make any final preparations before venturing into the gauntlet known as {{ho|Victory Road}}.

===Victory Road===
[[File:Victory Road 1F RS.png|thumb|Victory Road, 1F]]
[[File:Victory Road B1F RS.png|thumb|Victory Road, B1F]]
[[File:Victory Road B2F RS.png|thumb|Victory Road, B2F]]

{{ho|Victory Road}}, the long and grueling tunnel through the mountainside, is the final challenge on the road to the {{ho|Pokémon League}}. Like the waterfall outside, it helps ensure that only the strongest and most determined Trainers make it through to the other side. The field moves {{m|Surf}}, {{m|Strength}}, {{m|Rock Smash}}, and {{m|Waterfall}} are required to reach the exit, and dimly-lit areas make {{m|Flash}} optional, as well.

